From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 04:32:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add x86_64 guest support to the native bridge guest libraries

Add the x86_64 counterparts of the per-arch pieces the guest linker,
libc and vdso need: the interceptable stub macro, the vdso trap
entries, the static TLS hooks and the libc stub list, plus their
Android.bp arch entries. The libc stub list is the riscv64 one without
the setjmp family: an x86_64 guest on an x86_64 host shares the CPU,
so bionic's own setjmp/longjmp are correct where a host implementation
would capture its trampoline's frame.

The stub body is movabs $0, %r11; jmp *%r11: an implementation patches
the imm64 to its trampoline; r11 is caller-saved and carries no
argument (rax holds the vector register count of variadic calls).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Patch-Reason: a native bridge running x86_64 guest code on an x86_64 host (ATL's identity engine) needs x86_64 builds of these guest libraries; the arch blocks and per-arch sources live inside these Android.bp modules, which no launcher, loader or environment setting can add
---
